GojiGif — End User Licence Agreement
====================================

Version 1.0 · Effective 29 August 2026

    DRAFT — NOT YET REVIEWED BY COUNSEL.

    This agreement was drafted internally to close a release blocker: GojiGif was
    being distributed as a signed commercial binary with no licence terms at all.
    It states the terms Wolfberry AB intends, but it has not been reviewed by a
    lawyer. Have it reviewed before the 1.0 release, in particular the liability
    and consumer-rights clauses, which are the ones most likely to need adjusting
    for the markets the app is sold or distributed in. Remove this notice once
    that review is done.

This End User Licence Agreement ("Agreement") is a legal agreement between you,
either an individual or a single legal entity ("you"), and Wolfberry AB, a company
registered in Sweden ("Wolfberry", "we", "us"), for the GojiGif software, including
its executable code, associated media and documentation ("the Software").

By installing, copying or using the Software you agree to be bound by this
Agreement. If you do not agree, do not install or use the Software.


1. Licence grant
----------------

Subject to your compliance with this Agreement, Wolfberry grants you a
non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable licence to install and use the Software
on devices you own or control, for your personal use or for the internal business
purposes of your organisation.


2. Restrictions
---------------

Except to the extent the following restrictions are prohibited by applicable law,
or expressly permitted by us in writing, you may not:

  a. distribute, sell, rent, lease, sublicense or otherwise make the Software
     available to third parties;

  b. modify, adapt or create derivative works of the Software;

  c. reverse engineer, decompile or disassemble the Software, or otherwise attempt
     to derive its source code;

  d. remove, obscure or alter any copyright, trademark or other proprietary notice
     in or on the Software; or

  e. use the Software to infringe the rights of others, or in breach of applicable
     law — including recording another person's screen, or content displayed on it,
     without the consent or legal basis that law requires.

Nothing in this section limits any right you have under mandatory law that cannot
be excluded by agreement. In particular, nothing here restricts acts of
decompilation permitted under Article 6 of Directive 2009/24/EC on the legal
protection of computer programs, or the corresponding provisions of Swedish law.


3. Ownership
------------

The Software is licensed, not sold. Wolfberry and its licensors retain all right,
title and interest in and to the Software, including all intellectual property
rights in it. This Agreement grants you no rights other than the licence expressly
set out in section 1.


4. Your recordings
------------------

The Software records your screen and writes the result to your device as an
animated GIF. Those recordings are yours. Wolfberry claims no rights in them, and
this Agreement grants us no licence to them.

The Software transmits no data to Wolfberry or to any third party: it makes no
network requests, collects no telemetry and contains no analytics. See
docs/Privacy.md and the privacy policy published with the Software.

You are responsible for what you record. Screen recordings can capture personal
data, credentials and confidential material, and you are responsible for having any
consent or legal basis that recording and sharing them requires.


5. Third-party components
-------------------------

The Software includes components licensed by third parties, listed in
THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md, which is distributed with the Software. Those components
are governed by their own licence terms, which take precedence over this Agreement
in respect of those components.


6. Updates
----------

Wolfberry may make updates to the Software available. Unless an update is
accompanied by different terms, this Agreement applies to it. Wolfberry is under no
obligation to provide updates, support or maintenance.


7. No warranty
--------------

To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, the Software is provided "as
is" and "as available", without warranty of any kind, whether express, implied or
statutory, including any implied warranty of merchantability, fitness for a
particular purpose, or non-infringement. Wolfberry does not warrant that the
Software will be uninterrupted or error-free, or that it will capture or preserve
any particular recording.

If you are a consumer, you may have statutory rights that this section cannot
exclude or limit, and nothing in it affects those rights.


8. Limitation of liability
--------------------------

To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, Wolfberry shall not be liable
for any indirect, incidental, special or consequential damages, or for loss of
profits, revenue, data or recordings, arising out of or in connection with the
Software or this Agreement, however caused and on any theory of liability.

Wolfberry's total aggregate liability arising out of or in connection with the
Software or this Agreement shall not exceed the greater of the amount you paid for
the Software in the twelve months preceding the event giving rise to the claim, or
one hundred (100) euro.

Nothing in this Agreement excludes or limits liability for death or personal
injury caused by negligence, for fraud or fraudulent misrepresentation, for gross
negligence or wilful misconduct, or for any other liability that cannot lawfully be
excluded or limited.


9. Term and termination
-----------------------

This Agreement applies from the moment you first install or use the Software until
terminated. It terminates automatically if you breach any of its terms. On
termination you must stop using the Software and remove all copies of it from your
devices. Sections 3, 4, 5, 7, 8, 10 and 11 survive termination.


10. Governing law and jurisdiction
----------------------------------

This Agreement is governed by the laws of Sweden, without regard to its
conflict-of-laws rules. The courts of Sweden, with Stockholm District Court as the
court of first instance, shall have exclusive jurisdiction over any dispute arising
out of or in connection with it.

If you are a consumer resident in the European Union, this choice of law and forum
does not deprive you of the protection of mandatory provisions of the law of your
country of residence, or of your right to bring proceedings there.


11. General
-----------

This Agreement is the entire agreement between you and Wolfberry concerning the
Software, and supersedes any prior understanding relating to it. If any provision
is held unenforceable, it shall be modified to the minimum extent necessary to make
it enforceable, and the remaining provisions shall remain in full force. A failure
to enforce a provision is not a waiver of it. You may not assign this Agreement
without our prior written consent.


